<title>FRANCE: Rouen Nov grain exports rose year-on-year.</title>
<headline>Rouen Nov grain exports rose year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exports from Rouen jumped to 704,741 tonnes in November 1996 from 336,000 tonnes in November 1995, port officials said.</p>
<p>The 704,741 tonnes grain total included 641,298 tonnes of wheat, 62,143 tonnes of barley and 1,300 tonnes of maize destined for La Reunion island.</p>
<p>Officials gave the following breakdown by destination (in tonnes)</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    West Africa		     33,000</p>
<p>    Albania			    6,800</p>
<p>    Egypt			     92,636</p>
<p>    Britain			   18,945</p>
<p>    Ireland			    2,990</p>
<p>    Italy			    172,293</p>
<p>    Kuwait			    26,250</p>
<p>    Morocco			  100,050</p>
<p>    Poland			   116,514</p>
<p>    Portugal			   1,500</p>
<p>    Sudan			     27,500</p>
<p>    Turkey			    42,820</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Saudi Arabia		    55,000</p>
<p>    Greece			     2,750</p>
<p>    Italy				3,393</p>
<p>    West Africa			1,000</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
